3. The Augmented System

3.1 State

Definition 3.1 (Augmented state). The state is

Z_t = (X_t, \theta_t) \in \mathcal{Z} := \mathcal{X} \times \Theta_{\mathrm{epi}},

where X_t \in \mathcal{X} \subseteq \mathbb{R}^n is the physical state and \theta_t \in \Theta_{\mathrm{epi}} is the epistemic parameter.

Remark 3.1. \theta_t belongs to the state; the disturbance is \xi_t := w_t \in \mathcal{W}. The earlier double-count of \theta_t in both state and disturbance is not present.

3.2 Observation

Definition 3.2 (Observation map). With registration error \epsilon_t^{\mathrm{reg}} \in \mathcal{R} \subset \mathfrak{se}(3),

Y_t = H\bigl(Z_t, \mathbf{p}_t^{\mathrm{cmd}} \oplus \mathrm{Exp}(\epsilon_t^{\mathrm{reg}})\bigr) + \eta_t.

Remark 3.2. Registration error enters through the observation, not through the dynamics. If, in a specific instantiation, registration perturbs the physical dynamics (e.g., actuator frame misalignment), one must introduce a separate variable \delta_t^{\mathrm{act}} \in \mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{act}} and write F^\star(Z_t, u_t, w_t, \delta_t^{\mathrm{act}}).

3.3 Information State

Definition 3.3 (Information state).

\mathfrak{I}_t := (\mathcal{Z}_t, b_t, \Theta_t, \mathcal{W}, \mathcal{R}),

where \mathcal{Z}_t is the feasibility set, b_t is a belief distribution on \mathcal{Z}, and \Theta_t is the current epistemic uncertainty set.

Principle 3.1 (Policy on information state). The control policy is a measurable map

\pi : \mathfrak{I} \to \mathcal{U}, \qquad u_t = \pi(\mathfrak{I}_t).

---

4. The Four Maps

4.1 True Dynamics

F^\star : \mathcal{Z} \times \mathcal{U} \times \mathcal{W} \to \mathcal{Z}.

4.2 Certified Propagation

\widehat{F} : 2^{\mathcal{Z}} \times \mathcal{U} \to 2^{\mathcal{Z}}.

Interpretation. \widehat{F}(\mathcal{Z}, u) is a computationally tractable outer approximation of the true image F^\star(\mathcal{Z}, u, \mathcal{W}).

4.3 Measurement Contraction

\mathcal{E} : \mathcal{Y} \to 2^{\mathcal{Z}}.

Interpretation. \mathcal{E}(Y) is the set of states consistent with observation Y under the observation model.

4.4 Safe-Action Map

\mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}} : 2^{\mathcal{Z}} \to 2^{\mathcal{U}}, \qquad \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{A}) = \bigcap_{Z \in \mathcal{A} \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}} \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{CBF}}(Z).

4.5 The Update

Definition 4.1 (Feasibility update).

\boxed{\mathcal{Z}_{t+1} = \widehat{F}(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t) \cap \mathcal{E}(Y_{t+1}).}

