6. Derived Results

6.1 Update Soundness

Lemma 6.1 (Update Soundness). Under C1 and C2 (bounded mode), for any t \ge 0,

Z_{t+1}^\star \in \widehat{F}(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t) \;\land\; Y_{t+1} \in H(Z_{t+1}^\star) \oplus \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{obs}} \;\Longrightarrow\; Z_{t+1}^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_{t+1}.

Proof. By C1, Z_{t+1}^\star \in \widehat{F}(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t). By C2, Z_{t+1}^\star \in \mathcal{E}(Y_{t+1}). Intersecting:

Z_{t+1}^\star \in \widehat{F}(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t) \cap \mathcal{E}(Y_{t+1}) = \mathcal{Z}_{t+1}. \qquad \square

Remark 6.1. Lemma 6.1 is a derived lemma, not an independent contract. It depends on C1 and C2.

6.2 Safe-Action Soundness

Proposition 6.2 (Safe-Action Soundness — replaces contract C3). Let \mathcal{A} \subseteq \mathcal{Z} with \mathcal{A} \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}} \neq \emptyset. If u \in \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{A}), then

F^\star(\mathcal{A} \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}, u, \mathcal{W}) \subseteq \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}.

Proof. Identical to Proposition 2.5. □

Remark 6.2. In the deterministic composition proof below, the induction hypothesis gives Z_t^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_t \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}, so Proposition 6.2 applies directly with \mathcal{A} = \mathcal{Z}_t. No global requirement \mathcal{Z}_t \subseteq \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}} (Certificate D) is needed.

