7. Deterministic Composition Theorem

Theorem 7.1 (Deterministic Composition). Assume C0 (deterministic), C0′, C1, C2 (bounded mode), C4. Then for every finite horizon T \in \mathbb{N},

\boxed{Z_t^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_t \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}} \quad \forall t \in \{0, 1, \dots, T\}.}

Proof. By induction on t.

Base case (t=0). By C0, Z_0^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_0 \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}.

Inductive step. Assume Z_t^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_t \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}.

Choice of action. For t = 0, \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z}_0) \neq \emptyset by C0′. For t \ge 1, it holds by C4 applied at step t-1. Select u_t = \pi(\mathfrak{I}_t) \in \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z}_t).

Safety. Since Z_t^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_t \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}} and u_t \in \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z}_t), Proposition 6.2 gives

F^\star(\mathcal{Z}_t \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}, u_t, \mathcal{W}) \subseteq \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}.

Hence for every w_t \in \mathcal{W}, Z_{t+1}^\star = F^\star(Z_t^\star, u_t, w_t) \in \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}.

Propagation. By C1,

F^\star(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t, \mathcal{W}) \subseteq \widehat{F}(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t).

Since Z_t^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_t, we have Z_{t+1}^\star \in \widehat{F}(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t).

Containment. By C2 at t+1, since Y_{t+1} \in H(Z_{t+1}^\star) \oplus \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{obs}},

Z_{t+1}^\star \in \mathcal{E}(Y_{t+1}).

Therefore

Z_{t+1}^\star \in \widehat{F}(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t) \cap \mathcal{E}(Y_{t+1}) = \mathcal{Z}_{t+1}.

Combining with safety,

Z_{t+1}^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_{t+1} \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}.

By C4, \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z}_{t+1}) \neq \emptyset, permitting the induction to continue. □

Corollary 7.2. Under the hypotheses of Theorem 7.1,

\mathcal{Z}_t \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}} \neq \emptyset \quad \forall t \le T.

