13. Discussion and Open Problems

13.1 What Is Proven

1. Deterministic composition (Theorem 7.1). Under C0, C0′, C1, C2 (bounded mode), C4, the true state remains in \mathcal{Z}_t \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}} for all t \le T.
2. Probabilistic composition (Theorem 8.1). Under C0, C0′, C1, C2, C4, C5, C6, the same holds with probability at least 1 - \Delta, conditional on the standing event A = A_{\mathrm{CP}} \cap A_E.
3. Action-set monotonicity (Theorem 9.1). \mathcal{Z}_1 \subseteq \mathcal{Z}_2 \Rightarrow \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z}_2) \subseteq \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z}_1).
4. Agency index monotonicity (Corollary 9.4). \kappa_{\mathrm{agency}} is nonnegative and monotone under set inclusion when \mathcal{Z} \subseteq \mathcal{Z}_{\mathrm{ref}}.
5. Quantitative monotonicity (Proposition 9.5). Under Assumptions 9.A and 9.B, the agency loss \mu(\mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z})) - \mu(\mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z}_{\mathrm{ref}})) is bounded by \psi(L \cdot \mathrm{diam}(\mathcal{Z}_{\mathrm{ref}})).

13.2 What Is Assumed

The contracts C0, C0′, C1, C2, C4, C5, C6 are the framework's interface to physics. They must be established for each concrete instantiation.

· C0: initial feasibility and safety of Z_0^\star.
· C0′: initial action availability.
· C1: outer approximation soundness of \widehat{F}.
· C2: measurement contraction soundness.
· C4: recursive feasibility.
· C5: probabilistic containment under A.
· C6: safety budget.

13.3 Open Research Hypotheses

H9 (Latent Conformal Coverage).

\exists \mathfrak{D}, A_{\mathrm{CP}}, \mathrm{CP}^\star \text{ such that } \forall P \in \mathfrak{D}: P(Z_t^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_t \mid A_{\mathrm{CP}}) \ge 1 - \alpha_t - \varepsilon_t,

with \varepsilon_t supplied by the eventual theorem of \mathrm{CP}^\star.

H7 (Countermodel Obligation). Exhibit a property P provable in \mathfrak{A} using an explicit interface theorem, together with a countermodel M \models A_{\mathrm{components}} with M \not\models P, showing that the component axioms alone are insufficient.

H10 (Quantitative monotonicity without 9.A–9.B). Determine whether Proposition 9.5 admits a version in which the Lipschitz and level-set hypotheses are replaced by weaker semicontinuity or variational conditions on the CBF family.

13.4 What Is Killed

· General support equality \operatorname{supp}(b_t) = \mathcal{Z}_t.
· SOCP reduction from convexity alone.
· H7 as ablation theorem.
· Latent conformal coverage without assumptions.
· BCBF + conformal without temporal composition.
· "Certified contraction operator" as a non-trivial operator (it collapses to the identity).
· Identification of belief-support safety with probabilistic safety.
· \kappa as a metric.
· Use of C3 as a primitive contract (demoted to Proposition 6.2).

