Appendix D: Full Proof of Lemma 6.1 (Update Soundness)

Lemma 6.1. Under C1 and C2 (bounded mode), for any t \ge 0,

Z_{t+1}^\star \in \widehat{F}(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t) \;\land\; Y_{t+1} \in H(Z_{t+1}^\star) \oplus \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{obs}} \;\Longrightarrow\; Z_{t+1}^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_{t+1}.

Proof. Assume the two hypotheses.

(i) Propagation containment. From C1 applied to \mathcal{Z} = \mathcal{Z}_t and u = u_t,

F^\star(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t, \mathcal{W}) \subseteq \widehat{F}(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t).

If Z_t^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_t and w_t \in \mathcal{W}, then Z_{t+1}^\star = F^\star(Z_t^\star, u_t, w_t) \in F^\star(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t, \mathcal{W}) \subseteq \widehat{F}(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t). Hence

Z_{t+1}^\star \in \widehat{F}(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t). \tag{D.1}

(ii) Measurement containment. C2 (bounded mode) states that Y_t \in H(Z_t) \oplus \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{obs}} implies Z_t \in \mathcal{E}(Y_t). Applying this at time t+1 to the second hypothesis,

Z_{t+1}^\star \in \mathcal{E}(Y_{t+1}). \tag{D.2}

(iii) Intersection. Combining (D.1) and (D.2) and using the definition of the feasibility update (Definition 4.1),

Z_{t+1}^\star \in \widehat{F}(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t) \cap \mathcal{E}(Y_{t+1}) = \mathcal{Z}_{t+1}. \qquad \square

Remark D.1 (Role of the two hypotheses). The first hypothesis Z_{t+1}^\star \in \widehat{F}(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t) is not automatic: it requires Z_t^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_t, which the induction supplies. The second hypothesis Y_{t+1} \in H(Z_{t+1}^\star) \oplus \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{obs}} is the bounded-noise assumption on the observation channel.

Remark D.2 (Independence from the safe-action map). Lemma 6.1 does not use \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}, \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}, or h. It is a purely set-theoretic statement about propagation and measurement.

