Appendix E: Full Proof of Theorem 7.1 (Deterministic Composition)

Theorem 7.1. Assume C0 (deterministic), C0′, C1, C2 (bounded mode), C4. Then for every finite horizon T \in \mathbb{N},

Z_t^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_t \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}} \quad \forall t \in \{0, 1, \dots, T\}.

Proof. By induction on t. We establish the conjunction

P(t) : \quad Z_t^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_t \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}} \;\land\; \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z}_t) \neq \emptyset.

The second conjunct is needed for the inductive step at time t (to select u_t) and is supplied by C0′ at t=0 and by C4 for t \ge 1.

Base case t=0.

Safety and containment. By C0 (deterministic),

Z_0^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_0 \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}. \tag{E.1}

Action availability. By C0′,

\mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z}_0) \neq \emptyset. \tag{E.2}

Together, (E.1) and (E.2) establish P(0).

Inductive step. Assume P(t) for some t \ge 0. We establish P(t+1).

Choice of action. Since \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z}_t) \neq \emptyset by the second conjunct of P(t), select

u_t = \pi(\mathfrak{I}_t) \in \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z}_t). \tag{E.3}

Safety of the successor. By the first conjunct of P(t), Z_t^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_t \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}. By (E.3), u_t \in \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z}_t). Proposition 2.5 applies with \mathcal{A} = \mathcal{Z}_t:

F^\star(\mathcal{Z}_t \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}, u_t, \mathcal{W}) \subseteq \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}. \tag{E.4}

Since Z_t^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_t \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}} and w_t \in \mathcal{W},

Z_{t+1}^\star = F^\star(Z_t^\star, u_t, w_t) \in F^\star(\mathcal{Z}_t \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}, u_t, \mathcal{W}) \subseteq \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}. \tag{E.5}

Propagation containment. By C1 applied to \mathcal{Z} = \mathcal{Z}_t, u = u_t,

F^\star(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t, \mathcal{W}) \subseteq \widehat{F}(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t).

Since Z_t^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_t and w_t \in \mathcal{W},

Z_{t+1}^\star \in \widehat{F}(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t). \tag{E.6}

Measurement containment. The observation model Y_{t+1} = H(Z_{t+1}^\star) + \eta_{t+1} with \eta_{t+1} \in \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{obs}} gives Y_{t+1} \in H(Z_{t+1}^\star) \oplus \mathcal{V}_{\mathrm{obs}}. By C2 (bounded mode),

Z_{t+1}^\star \in \mathcal{E}(Y_{t+1}). \tag{E.7}

Feasibility at t+1. Intersecting (E.6) and (E.7),

Z_{t+1}^\star \in \widehat{F}(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t) \cap \mathcal{E}(Y_{t+1}) = \mathcal{Z}_{t+1}. \tag{E.8}

Together with (E.5),

Z_{t+1}^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_{t+1} \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}. \tag{E.9}

Action availability at t+1. By C4 applied at step t to \mathcal{Z}_t,

\mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z}_{t+1}) \neq \emptyset. \tag{E.10}

Combining (E.9) and (E.10) establishes P(t+1).

Conclusion. By induction, P(t) holds for all t \in \{0, 1, \dots, T\}. In particular, Z_t^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_t \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}} for all t \le T. □

Corollary 7.2. Under the hypotheses of Theorem 7.1,

\mathcal{Z}_t \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}} \neq \emptyset \quad \forall t \le T.

Proof. Immediate from Z_t^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_t \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}} established in Theorem 7.1. □

Remark E.1 (Role of C0′). C0′ is essential and cannot be derived from C0 or C4. C0 gives safety and containment of the true state at t=0 but says nothing about \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z}_0). C4 is a conditional implication and cannot bootstrap nonemptiness. Without C0′, the induction cannot start.

Remark E.2 (Role of C4). C4 is applied at step t to yield \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z}_{t+1}) \neq \emptyset. It is not used to establish safety of Z_{t+1}^\star (which comes from Proposition 2.5) nor containment (which comes from C1 and C2).

Remark E.3 (Removal of C3). In v1.2, the proof invoked C3 to conclude F^\star(\mathcal{Z}_t, u_t, \mathcal{W}) \subseteq \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}. As noted in the critical review, this is not justifiable when \mathcal{Z}_t \not\subseteq \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}, because the CBF inequality weakens for h(Z) < 0. The revised proof uses only Proposition 2.5, which restricts the intersection to \mathcal{Z}_t \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}, and the induction hypothesis Z_t^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_t \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}}. No global Certificate D is required.

