Appendix K: Summary of the Composition Theorem

Deterministic.

\boxed{\text{C0} + \text{C0}′ + \text{C1} + \text{C2} + \text{C4} \;\Longrightarrow\; Z_t^\star \in \mathcal{Z}_t \cap \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}} \;\; \forall t \le T.}

Probabilistic.

\boxed{\text{C0} + \text{C0}′ + \text{C1} + \text{C2} + \text{C4} + \text{C5} + \text{C6} \;\Longrightarrow\; P\bigl(Z_t^\star \in \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}} \; \forall t \le T \mid A\bigr) \ge 1 - \Delta.}

Unconditionally, if P(A^c) \le \rho, the bound is 1 - \Delta - \rho.

Structural (order-theoretic).

\boxed{\mathcal{Z}_1 \subseteq \mathcal{Z}_2 \;\Longrightarrow\; \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z}_2) \subseteq \mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z}_1).}

Structural (quantitative).

\boxed{\mathcal{Z} \subseteq \mathcal{Z}_{\mathrm{ref}} \subseteq \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{safe}} \;\Longrightarrow\; 0 \le \mu(\mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z})) - \mu(\mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\mathcal{Z}_{\mathrm{ref}})) \le \psi(L \cdot \mathrm{diam}(\mathcal{Z}_{\mathrm{ref}})).}

These four statements constitute the mathematical core of the framework.

