M. Note on Search Coverage and Limitations

The bibliography above was assembled through systematic web searches across the following topical clusters:

1. Discrete-time CBFs — foundational and recent advances in sampled-data and discrete-time safety certificates.
2. Robust CBFs under uncertainty — state uncertainty, parametric uncertainty, and measurement-robust formulations.
3. Set-based reachability — polynomial zonotopes, interval reachability, and probabilistic reachable sets.
4. Set-membership estimation — contraction-theoretic and interval-observer approaches.
5. Conformal prediction in control — finite-sample coverage for safety filters and neural CBF verification.
6. Contract-based design — assume-guarantee contracts for cyber-physical systems.
7. Belief-space safety — BCBFs, POMDP barrier certificates, and belief-space planning under uncertainty.
8. Lipschitz regularity — safety verification via Lipschitz bounds on CBFs and neural networks.
9. Hamilton–Jacobi reachability — CBVFs and the bridge between HJ reachability and CBFs.

